From: Balázs Gyimesi <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mhi_net: copy small packets out of large RX buffers

With a large MRU (a modem sending aggregated QMAP frames) every RX buffer
is the MRU's size, and a plain 1.5 kB packet received into it carries the
whole buffer's truesize (over 32 KiB with the page backed buffers; the
mhi_net MTU plays no part in the RX buffer size, only the controller's MRU
does). A TCP socket on the host is charged that for each packet, its
receive window collapses, and, measured with 16 KiB buffers, a download on
the router itself dropped from ~100 Mbit/s to ~7 Mbit/s while forwarded
traffic was unaffected. Copy a small packet into a right-sized skb;
aggregated frames stay as they are.

The copy is skipped when an rx_handler is registered on the device (rmnet
on the QMAP link): rmnet's deaggregation already copies each packet out of
the frame into a right-sized skb, so the stack never sees the large
truesize, and a lone small packet would otherwise be copied twice.
rcu_access_pointer() is enough: the callback runs in the MHI event tasklet
with BH disabled, only the NULL/non-NULL state matters, and a stale read
around rmnet's attach or detach costs one copy more or less for one packet.
netdev_is_rx_handler_busy() cannot be used there (ASSERT_RTNL). The raw-IP
mode (no rmnet) keeps the copybreak as before; with the page backed
buffers the truesize test is always true, so that is the only mode the
copy happens in. This assumes the rmnet link deaggregates
(RMNET_FLAGS_INGRESS_DEAGGREGATION, which libqmi sets on every link it
creates); a link created without that flag hands the whole buffer to the
stack unchanged and would want the copy back.
---
--- a/drivers/net/mhi_net.c
+++ b/drivers/net/mhi_net.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/u64_stats_sync.h>
 
 #define MHI_NET_MIN_MTU		ETH_MIN_MTU
+#define MHI_NET_COPYBREAK	2048
 #define MHI_NET_MAX_MTU		0xffff
 #define MHI_NET_DEFAULT_MTU	0x4000
 
@@ -207,6 +208,26 @@
 			/* Aggregate the final fragment */
 			skb = mhi_net_skb_agg(mhi_netdev, skb);
 			mhi_netdev->skbagg_head = NULL;
+		} else if (skb->len <= MHI_NET_COPYBREAK &&
+			   skb->truesize > 2 * MHI_NET_COPYBREAK &&
+			   !rcu_access_pointer(mhi_netdev->ndev->rx_handler)) {
+			/* A large MRU (aggregated frames) with a small packet in
+			 * it: hand the stack a right-sized copy, or every 1.5 kB
+			 * packet charges the whole buffer's truesize (32 KiB) to
+			 * the receiving socket and shrinks its window. Not when a
+			 * receive handler is attached (rmnet in QMAP mode): it
+			 * deaggregates by copying every packet into a right-sized
+			 * skb, so the copy here would only be a second one. (An
+			 * rmnet link without INGRESS_DEAGGREGATION passes the
+			 * buffer through as is; libqmi always sets the flag.)
+			 */
+			struct sk_buff *small = netdev_alloc_skb(mhi_netdev->ndev, skb->len);
+
+			if (small) {
+				skb_put_data(small, skb->data, skb->len);
+				dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+				skb = small;
+			}
 		}
 
 		switch (skb->data[0] & 0xf0) {
